  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "# Changelog\n\n## 0.2.1 — 2026-10-26\n\nThe README only; the code is unchanged from 0.2.0.\n\n- The Connections page that has your credentials and the signature checker is now called **Your\n  code** (it was HTTP API), and the README says so. Robovue's home page is now called Home.\n\n## 0.2.0 — 2026-10-18\n\nThe first public release.\n\n- `ReportRunAsync` reports a run, signed with Robovue's v1 scheme: the signature covers a\n  timestamp, the endpoint and the delivery id as well as the body, so a captured request can't be\n  replayed and stops working after five minutes. Every retry is signed afresh.\n- `TryReportRunAsync` reports a run without ever throwing, so monitoring can't break the bot. Why a\n  report failed is in `RunReportOutcome.Error`.\n- `RunStatus.Running` and a reused delivery id report a run that's still going, then its outcome.\n  `RunReportResult.DeliveryId` gives back the id that was sent.\n- `UploadAttachmentAsync` attaches a screenshot or log to a failed run.\n- `RobovueClientOptions.DryRun` checks every request in full and stores nothing; the result's\n  `DryRun` and `WouldBe` say what would have happened.\n- `RobovueApiException` carries the server's `Code`, `Field` and `RequestId`.\n- Network errors and 5xx responses are retried with backoff, and a `429` after its `Retry-After`\n  (a wait over one minute is thrown instead of blocking the bot).\n- Reports are checked against the server's own rules before sending: names, times, categories, the\n  payload, the 64 KB limit and the delivery id.\n- Targets netstandard2.0 and net8.0, strong-named, with XML docs.",
  "verbatimVersion": "0.2.1",
